Here’s the problem:

fetchLastLogin() gets called inside the useEffect.

The effect depends on [fetched, isAuthenticated, isLoading].

However, on initial mount, React may run this effect twice in Strict Mode (used by default in development mode via React.StrictMode) — not a bug, but a feature to help detect side effects.

Hence, you see two calls to getLastLogin(), which inserts two records.

